Z||000026||Seanh||10-29-2000||06:08 PM||||Oh well, I am just going to do the front for now, with the beretta rotors and calipers. I will let you know how it turns out. I am not much for racing, but I do have a lead foot. Would it be okay to switch to the S-10 SC if I just do the front? Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/singnit.gif"> <BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000027||theogre||10-29-2000||09:56 PM||||You may not need the bigger master cyl if you only do the front. Do the calipers and see how the pedal feels. No sence putting on a diferant MC unless you're sure you want/need it.<P>This is alot up to personal preference in a front only upgrade. If you feel the pedal travels to much for you then you could do the lager MC. Do note tho that a larger MC will also affect brake function. (Larger MC = smaller Master/Slave ratio = More force at pedal to do the same work.) It will affect both front and rear but I expect more affect on the rear.||||reg||1
